                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "A recent report from the @USCBO confirms what we already knew \u2013 the partisan budget passed last month funds tax breaks to the wealthiest households by slashing critical health care and nutrition programs that everyday families in South Texas rely on.\n\nWhile the top 10% will receive $13,600 more annually, the lowest 10% of earners will lose $1,200 every year largely due to cuts to Medicaid and SNAP. These cuts mean fewer people will get the care and food assistance they need, making it harder for working families, seniors, and the most vulnerable to make ends meet.\n\nInstead of protecting essential services, this budget takes from those who can least afford it to reward those who need it least, which is why I voted against these dangerous cuts. I'll continue fighting for responsible, bipartisan solutions that strengthen our economy and put the needs of South Texan families first.",
                "text_lang": "en",
