                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "This morning, I visited the Zapata County Nutrition Center to meet with staff and local seniors and learn more about the services they provide.\n\nThe center plays a vital role in supporting the community through daily meals, home-delivered meals, transportation services, and wellness programs. These efforts are made possible through federal funding from the Older Americans Act, along with support from Zapata County. Thank you to Judge Olga Bruni, Nutrition Center Director Bertha Lopez, and all the staff who work every day to make these services possible.\n\nAs a member of the Appropriations Committee, I will continue working to secure funding and support programs that strengthen rural communities and provide vital services for elderly residents and families across South Texas.",
